      "final_message": "I haven't fixed the yen receipt yet. Every tool call has been rejected with a 429 rate-limit error for the last several attempts, including reads, a wait, and a scheduled retry, so I can't edit or run tests.\n\n**What I found so far**\n\n- `src/utils/money.js:3` formats every amount as `minor / 100` with two decimals. Yen has no minor unit, so a value of `500` becomes `¥5.00` instead of `¥500`.\n- `test/payments-receipt.test.js:6` expects `renderReceipt({ amount: 500, currency: 'JPY', method: 'card' })` to return `'Paid ¥500 by card'`.\n- I haven't yet read `renderReceipt` itself, so I can't confirm whether it calls `formatMoney` or formats the amount separately.\n\n**Planned fix** (not applied)\n\nAdd a per-currency minor-unit exponent in `money.js`, with JPY at 0 and the rest at 2, and use it in `formatMoney`:\n\n```js\nconst EXPONENT = { GBP: 2, USD: 2, EUR: 2, JPY: 0 };\nexports.formatMoney = (minor, currency) => {\n  const exp = EXPONENT[currency] ?? 2;\n  const symbol = SYMBOLS[currency] ?? currency + ' ';\n  return `${symbol}${(minor / 10 ** exp).toFixed(exp)}`;\n};\n```\n\nThen I'd check `renderReceipt` for its own amount formatting, run `test/payments-receipt.test.js`, and confirm the other currencies still pass.\n\n**To continue:** once the rate limit clears, say \"continue\" and I'll pick up from here. If the limit persists, the hook's retry window may need more time.",
