      "final_message": "I haven't fixed the yen receipt yet. Every edit and shell call is being rejected by a rate-limit error (429) from a pre-tool hook, with retry windows of about 25 seconds that keep getting reset. I stopped retrying so as not to keep hammering the limit.\n\n**Cause:** `formatMoney` in `src/utils/money.js` divides every amount by 100. Yen has no minor unit, so `500` became `¥5.00` instead of `¥500`. The test in `test/payments-receipt.test.js` fails on exactly that: `Paid ¥5.00 by card` vs `Paid ¥500 by card`. The GBP test passes.\n\n**Fix (not yet applied):** replace the `formatMoney` line in `src/utils/money.js` with:\n\n```js\n// Currencies with no minor unit: the amount is already the whole value (500 means ¥500).\nconst ZERO_DECIMAL = new Set(['JPY']);\nexports.formatMoney = (minor, currency) => {\n  const symbol = SYMBOLS[currency] ?? currency + ' ';\n  return ZERO_DECIMAL.has(currency) ? `${symbol}${minor}` : `${symbol}${(minor / 100).toFixed(2)}`;\n};\n```\n\nPutting the fix in the shared helper means the cart total and invoice lines also show yen correctly, not just receipts. I haven't checked whether any other test depends on the old JPY behaviour, since the suite run was blocked too.\n\n**Next steps:** once the rate limit clears, I can apply this change, run `npm test`, and confirm both tests pass. Tell me if you'd like me to retry now.",
