      "final_message": "The yen receipt fix isn't applied yet. Every edit and test run has been rejected by a 429 rate limit, and the retry window keeps moving, so `src/utils/money.js` is still unchanged.\n\n**Cause:** `formatMoney` in `src/utils/money.js` divides every amount by 100. That's right for GBP, USD and EUR, but yen has no minor unit, so 500 yen prints as `¥5.00`. The receipt, invoice and cart-total code all call this one function, so the bug affects all of them.\n\n**Fix:** replace the `formatMoney` line in `src/utils/money.js` with a zero-decimal check for JPY:\n\n```js\n// Currencies with no minor unit: the amount is already the whole currency value.\nconst ZERO_DECIMAL = new Set(['JPY']);\nexports.formatMoney = (minor, currency) => {\n  const symbol = SYMBOLS[currency] ?? currency + ' ';\n  if (ZERO_DECIMAL.has(currency)) return `${symbol}${minor}`;\n  return `${symbol}${(minor / 100).toFixed(2)}`;\n};\n```\n\nBefore the change, the suite reported 18 tests with 17 passing and 1 failing (the yen receipt test, `Paid ¥5.00 by card` vs `Paid ¥500 by card`). I haven't run it since the change, so the post-fix result is not yet verified.\n\nNext step: once the rate limit clears, I can apply this, run `node --test`, and commit if you want. Or you can paste the snippet in yourself now. I haven't committed anything.",
